{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEpic `inferior-seaborgium-aruanas` needs a `releases` field in compiled ticket state before any sync or surface can use it. Today compiled state has no release field (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:28-89`, `make_initial_state`), and no replayed event can change one. ADR 0124 (sibling ADR child) fixes the design: a list of Jira version names, carried by a new `RELEASE_DELTA` event with `TAG_DELTA`'s fold semantics, and `SCHEMA_VERSION` 6.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Event type.** In `src/rebar/reducer/_version.py`, add a single-source constant `RELEASE_DELTA = \"RELEASE_DELTA\"` beside `TAG_DELTA` (line 77), add it to `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` (lines 88-123), and bump `SCHEMA_VERSION` from 5 to 6 (line 41), with a comment naming ADR 0124.\n2. **Fold.** In `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, add `process_release_delta(state, data)` next to `process_tag_delta` (lines 429-449). It reads and writes `state[\"releases\"]` with the same rules: non-list `added`/`removed` act as empty; non-string or empty names are skipped; removals apply first, then additions, so a name in both lists stays; a repeated fold is idempotent. To avoid a second copy of the loop, extract the body of `process_tag_delta` into a private `_fold_list_delta(state, key, data)` and have both processors call it. `process_tag_delta` keeps its behavior exactly; its existing tests in `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_tag_delta.py` are the guard.\n3. **Dispatch.** Register `RELEASE_DELTA: lambda c: process_release_delta(c.state, c.data)` in the replay dispatch table in `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py` (beside line 109).\n4. **Default.** Add `\"releases\": []` to `make_initial_state` (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py`), right after `\"tags\"`. `make_error_dict` builds on it, so error states carry the key too.\n5. **Write path.** Add `RELEASE_DELTA` to `EVENT_TYPES` in `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` (the allow-list at lines 33-60) and to the allowed-types message (line 125), so the store accepts the event. Add `\"RELEASE_DELTA\"` to `_AUTO_RECOVER_ORPHAN_TYPES` in `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py:37-39` (additive types whose orphans allow a full-log rebuild), where `TAG_DELTA` already sits.\n6. **Snapshot.** No compaction change is needed: compaction stores the reduced state as `SNAPSHOT.compiled_state` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:688-705`) and `process_snapshot` restores every key it carries (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:464-468`). A snapshot written before this change has no `releases` key, so the restored state keeps the `[]` default.\n7. **Schema.** Add an optional `releases` property (array of strings, description naming ADR 0124) to `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`; do not add it to `required`, because pre-feature snapshots and older readers lack it. Regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` with `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types` (the CI check is `--check`).\n8. **Docs.** In `docs/event-schema.md`, add a `RELEASE_DELTA` row to the replayed-event table (beside the `TAG_DELTA` row at line 46), and record v6 in the \"Schema version & forward compatibility\" history: a new event body type, so older clones preserve and ignore it, and the reconcile host is upgraded first.\n\nNo writer of `RELEASE_DELTA` exists after this change except tests; the inbound, outbound and surface children add writers.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_version.py` (constant, known types, schema version)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` (shared list-delta fold, `process_release_delta`)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py` (dispatch)\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_state.py` (default)\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` (write allow-list)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py` (append-only type set)\n- `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`, `src/rebar/types.py` (generated)\n- `docs/event-schema.md`\n- `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_release_delta.py` (new)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py` (extend)\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_delta_store.py` (new: store append and compaction)\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_release_delta.py`, in the style of `test_reducer_tag_delta.py`:\n- happy path: `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"]}` then `{\"added\": [\"2.5\"], \"removed\": [\"2.4\"]}` reduces to `[\"2.5\"]`;\n- add beats remove in one event: `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"], \"removed\": [\"2.4\"]}` yields `[\"2.4\"]`;\n- idempotent: the same `{\"added\": [\"2.4\"]}` delta written twice (two events) yields `[\"2.4\"]`, and a remove of an absent name changes nothing;\n- two concurrent adds from different clones both survive;\n- malformed bodies (`added: \"2.4\"`, `added: [1, \"\"]`) leave `[]` without raising;\n- no `RELEASE_DELTA` events yields `releases == []`, and a `RELEASE_DELTA` leaves `tags` unchanged;\n- a pre-feature `SNAPSHOT` (no `releases` key) followed by a `RELEASE_DELTA` yields the delta's names;\n- a reducer with `RELEASE_DELTA` masked out of `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` ignores it without error (older-clone preserve-and-ignore, as `test_downgraded_clone_preserves_and_ignores` does for tags).\n\nNew `tests/interfaces/store/test_release_delta_store.py`, in the style of `tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_run_state.py`:\n- `_seam.append_event(tid, \"RELEASE_DELTA\", {...})` succeeds through the store write path (this fails if `event_prepare.EVENT_TYPES` lacks the type) and `rebar.show_ticket` returns the names;\n- `rebar store compact <tid> --threshold=0` writes a `SNAPSHOT` whose `compiled_state.releases` holds the names, and a later `show_ticket` returns the same list.\n\nExtend `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py`: `RELEASE_DELTA` is in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` and `SCHEMA_VERSION == 6`. The existing parity test in that file (`test_known_event_types_equals_the_reducer_dispatch_table`) pins the dispatch registration, and the existing `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_snapshot_checks.py:122` (fsck orphan sets must cover every known type except CREATE and SNAPSHOT) pins the fsck edit. The existing `test_reducer_tag_delta.py` must pass unchanged, which pins the extraction in step 2.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make_initial_state()[\"releases\"] == []`; pinned by the no-event reducer test.\n- [ ] A `RELEASE_DELTA` applies removals before additions, with an add winning when one name is in both lists; pinned by the happy-path and add-wins tests.\n- [ ] Repeating a `RELEASE_DELTA` changes nothing; pinned by the idempotency test.\n- [ ] A `RELEASE_DELTA` never changes `tags`; pinned by the no-leak test.\n- [ ] `SNAPSHOT` compaction preserves `releases`; pinned by the store compaction test.\n- [ ] A pre-feature snapshot replays to `[]` and then accepts later deltas; pinned by the pre-feature snapshot test.\n- [ ] The store accepts a `RELEASE_DELTA` append; pinned by the store append test.\n- [ ] `RELEASE_DELTA` is in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES` and `SCHEMA_VERSION == 6`; pinned by the forward-compat contract test.\n- [ ] `RELEASE_DELTA` is in fsck's auto-recover orphan set; pinned by `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_snapshot_checks.py`.\n- [ ] A reducer without `RELEASE_DELTA` in its known types ignores the event; pinned by the masked-reducer test.\n- [ ] `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_tag_delta.py` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` has a `RELEASE_DELTA` row and a v6 history entry.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794280889353442001,"uuid":"9f9abcd5-ebb2-4892-8d46-80d9c9c29044"}